WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.100
Good Morning, John

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.720
or rather, complicated morning John,

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.900
'cause stuff's been going down this week.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.640
As you know the state of 
North Carolina, where our parents live,

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.780
just decided to just outright ban gay marriage like stick it in the constitution

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.000
Opposing gay marriage is not 
a viewpoint that I understand.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.100
And I know this video is going to 
piss people off, but I don't care anymore.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:27.120
This isn't a political issue, it's just deciding that we're going to treat some citizens of our country differently than other citizens. That's wrong.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.440
So I want to go through 
some of the arguments that I hear

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.120
and why they're crazy!  ONE, what's the big deal,

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.280
why can't gay people just, you know, have a party and say they're committed to each other.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.680
Why do they gotta come in on our thing?

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.460
Irrelevant.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.080
This isn't complicated. If some people can get married, and other people can't

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.060
then that's wrong.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.680
TWO: But...God!?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.680
Marriage can be a religious thing.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.820
It can also be a secular thing. And guess what!

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.060
Not everyone in the world is of the same religion.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.060
Preventing gay people from getting married

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.680
is not an expression of religious freedom

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.940
It's an expression of religious oppression

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.680
Cause in the religion of the gay people

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.680
getting married, presumably

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.220
their God thinks it's okay. And you are oppressing them

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:15.700
"But...The Bible" The Bible is not a legal document. Our country was founded upon the idea of a separation between church and state.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:23.120
The Bible is also very explicit about the rules of farmers selling their daughters as slaves. So maybe not the best document to base our laws on.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:31.520
"Gay marriage would undermine the institution of marriage" This is a thing that I have named; I've created a name for it in my head, because I see them all the time.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:40.580
I'm calling them hypothetheories. So a hypothesis is a question that you ask. You say, 'I wonder if gay marriage would undermine the institution of marriage'.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:45.180
That's a hypothesis, that you can then go out and test in any number of ways.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.440
And then if you confirm that it is true and it explains phenomena, then you can eventually convert that into a theory.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:58.360
If you skip the middle step and just assume that now you have a true statement of fact, theory, then you have created what I call a hypothetheory.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:04.320
I could make the exact opposite hypothesis and it would be just as valid because it would have just as much testing behind it.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:11.860
I could say that not a lot of people who love each other to get married, that is undermining the institution of marriage. That seems like a valid thing, now let's go test it.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:19.860
So stop saying this as if it is truth, because you just made it up and you're like, "Oh! That makes sense to me! Why does that make so much sense to me, it does!

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:28.860
Whatever! It must be true! Make sense!" And you know why it makes sense? It's because of the biggest actual complaint that people have about gay marriage which is:

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:38.020
"It's unnatural. It doesn't feel right to me." And maybe to you, it doesn't seem right because we build our world, we build the rules of the world that we live in.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:46.740
That's how we understand this place. And I think to a lot people, it feels like this is a big messy, gray world and at least there are some sharp distinctions.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:52.620
Like the distinctions between genders and sexual orientation and those are just lines that should always be hard lines,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:59.700
but saying that that simplicity is natural is idiotic because the most natural thing in the world is complexity,

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.380
and gender and sexual orientation are proven over and over again to not be firm lines.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:11.140
The whole world is gray and if you just appreciate that, if you just understand that and appreciate that, then it's beautiful.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:17.220
But if you try and spend your whole life fighting against it, then you are going to be bitter about the world actually being more complicated than it is

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.880
and you're gonna make other people's lives less awesome. Which is exactly what this boils down to.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:31.220
Because there are a hundred arguments against gay marriage, you could come up with all kinds of hypothetheories and just spout them off and people will say, "Nod nod yes yes yes".

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:37.400
But to me there is only one argument that matters for gay marriage. That all people in our country should be seen as equals in the eyes of the law.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:48.360
So North Carolina and all of the 30 other states that have passed laws like this, you better check yourself because we can't live in a society like that and call ourselves Americans.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.360
John, I will see you on Tuesday.

